      "text": "The area of the parallelogram generated by vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by the magnitude of their cross product: $|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}|$. The cross product of $\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$ is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i}(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)) - \\mathbf{j}(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1) + \\mathbf{k}(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i}(4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j}(12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k}(-9 - 1) = -2\\mathbf{i} - 14\\mathbf{j} - 10\\mathbf{k} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of the cross product is:\n\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the parallelogram is $\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}$.",
